    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0564" n="536" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg536"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> UNP files, lot 59 D 237, “Slates”</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Director of the Office of
                        United Nations Political and Security Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Popper</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d307-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-30">April 30, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>Subject:</item>
                    <item>Ninth GA Presidency</item>
                </list>
                <p>It is UNA’s position that we should decide now to support Van Kleffens for the
                    presidency of the ninth GA and so advise the Netherlands Government. Attached is
                    a draft cable to the Secretary requesting his concurrence in this position.
                    Could we please have your clearance or comment on the draft as soon as
                        possible.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d307-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d307-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d307-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the four representatives of the geographic bureaus—Monsma (ARA),
                    Allen (EUR), Howard (NEA) and Bacon (FE)—who together with a representative from
                    the Bureau of UN Affairs constituted the Department of State’s (United Nations)
                    Membership Team.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d307-f2" n="2" xml:id="d307-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably no action was taken because of the arrival of Ambassador Lodge’
                    telegram 678, Apr. 30, 6 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
